# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — the important part.
#
# `.env*` covers .env, .env.local, .env.production and friends, so a real key
# can't be committed by accident. The negation below re-includes the example
# file, which contains only placeholders and belongs in the repo.
#
# Note the ordering: the negation MUST come after the pattern it overrides,
# otherwise `.env*` wins and .env.example silently never gets committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.next/
/out/
/build
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Testing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/coverage

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
dev.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated resume artifacts
#
# Exports are rendered on demand from a stored snapshot, so a stray PDF/DOCX in
# the working tree is a local test artifact — and one that would contain real
# personal details if committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/exports/
/tmp/
*.local.pdf
*.local.docx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Platform / editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vercel
.netlify
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UI audit output (scripts/ui-audit.mts) — regenerated on demand, never committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/screenshots/
/.playwright/
.playwright-mcp/
# Browser-verification output from ad-hoc audit runs, same as /screenshots above.
/shots-hdr/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent worktrees. Each carries its own node_modules, and eslint already ignores
# this path for the same reason: one left behind after a merge turned a clean
# lint run into 1,310 errors in code this project did not write.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.*/
!/.github/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# drizzle-kit's output directory (`out` in drizzle.config.ts).
#
# This project applies schema changes with `npm run db:push`, which writes no
# migration files — so the only thing that ever appears here is an empty
# meta/_journal.json left behind by `drizzle-kit check`/`studio`. It is a
# byproduct, not state, and it kept showing up as an untracked change.
#
# If migrations are ever adopted (`drizzle-kit generate`, i.e. a db:generate
# script alongside db:push), DELETE this rule — the generated SQL and its
# journal are real source and must be committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/drizzle/
